We go into the bright kitchen together.
It smells incredibly good here.
Nele is cooking a curry with lots of vegetables.
She stands at the stove and stirs the pot.
"The main course is almost ready," says Nele.
"I just have to cut the fresh herbs."
I immediately go over to her.
"I help you," I say.
"What can I do?"
"Oh, gladly!" she answers.
"I think that cooking together is always fun."
Nele opens a small drawer.
She gives me a small knife and a cutting board.
Then she lays fresh coriander on the table.
I wash the coriander and cut it into small pieces.
"The food will certainly taste very delicious," I say.
"I hope that you like spicy food," Nele laughs.
I smile and nod.
As a Mexican, I naturally like spicy food very much!
